[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) went in as one issue: dates parse mm/dd in eu locales. Read report by
report, it holds three problems with three different fixes. Each one now has its own ticket.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

<Callout kind="warn">
Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October. That closes two of the three problems: the parser is
fixed, and the form hint will not be fixed because booking-v3 is retired. The one-day move has
no fix, and its ticket stays open.
</Callout>

## Where each problem stands

| problem | ticket | state | why |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| parser | [#1](https://github.com/melvinsalvador/support-kb-4471/issues/1) | closed · fixed | `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` |
| form hint | [#2](https://github.com/melvinsalvador/support-kb-4471/issues/2) | closed · won't fix | booking-v3 form retired |
| one-day move | [#3](https://github.com/melvinsalvador/support-kb-4471/issues/3) | **open** | not part of the #4471 fix |

## The three problems

**Parser** ([#1](https://github.com/melvinsalvador/support-kb-4471/issues/1)). The shared parser
reads every date month first, and every tenant in #4471 writes the day first. "Booked for
7 April" comes back as 4 July. It reaches us through the app, email and the booking-v2 form.

**Form hint** ([#2](https://github.com/melvinsalvador/support-kb-4471/issues/2)). booking-v3
prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, and its tenants read the field day first. People type
what the hint tells them, so the date flips. These reports come only through the form, only from
the three tenants on booking-v3. A parser fix does not touch them.

**One-day move** ([#3](https://github.com/melvinsalvador/support-kb-4471/issues/3)). Not a flip:
the date lands a day early, or differs by where the person is. "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday.
Client in Toronto got Monday." That is a time-zone conversion. The desk already read these as a
one-day move (`desk-notes.json`). They stay filed and counted under the parser, by tenant, the
way the cause table counts them, and #3 tracks them as their own bug.

## Why one ticket hid three

- **We merged on subject.** [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports
  whose subjects match. "Wrong day on the invite" fits all three problems, so all three landed in
  one ticket.
- **Intake guesses from the browser.** The intake tag comes from the reporter's browser, not the
  tenant, so it misfiles form-hint reports as parser ones and the other way round. The table
  above asks the tenant directory instead.
- **The export repeats rows.** The ticket system exports in overlapping pages. Counts here are by
  unique report id.

